{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:102218",
  "title": "Important: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-25 06:01:11"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-28 00:04:27"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: ALSA: caiaq: fix out-of-bounds read in the Traktor Kontrol S4 input parser (CVE-2026-64487)\n\n* kernel: scsi: target: Bound PR-OUT TransportID parsing to the received buffer (CVE-2026-72084)\n\n* kernel: RDMA/srpt: fix integer overflow in immediate data length check (CVE-2026-74394)\n\n* kernel: RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in ib_free_cq() (CVE-2026-92508)\n\n* kernel: uio: Fix stale info pointer in failed registration path (CVE-2026-93054)\n\n* kernel: RDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in ib_destroy_cq_user() (CVE-2026-92511)\n\n* kernel: IB/isert: reject login PDUs declaring more data than was received (CVE-2026-90413)\n\n* kernel: IB/isert: reject PDUs declaring more data than was received (CVE-2026-90414)\n\n* kernel: IB/isert: delay the final Login Response until the session is registered (CVE-2026-90294)\n\n* kernel: tcp: prevent collapsing skbs across boundary in rtx queue (CVE-2026-98549)\n\n* kernel: kernel: Privilege escalation via use-after-free in event tracing subsystem (CVE-2026-99235)\n\n* kernel: kernel: Denial of Service via race condition in TCP socket lookup (CVE-2026-99288)\n\n* kernel: kernel: Memory corruption via integer overflow in GUP-fast (CVE-2026-99661)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* [Rocky Linux-8.10.z] RDMA/ulps: Backport security fixes (JIRA:Rocky Linux-289994)\n\n* [Rocky Linux-8.10.z] RDMA: Backport security fixes (JIRA:Rocky Linux-296076)\n\n* [Rocky Linux 8.10] Incorrect swap size value in /proc/swaps if swap area is very big (JIRA:Rocky Linux-302561)\n\n* lockd: fix vfs_test_lock() calls (JIRA:Rocky Linux-304667)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
